{"units": [{"id": "anagke-word2", "translation": "by other constraints or fearing someone's wrath"}, {"id": "anagke-word3", "translation": "necessity"}, {"id": "anagke-word4", "translation": "it is necessary"}, {"id": "anagkadakrys-orth1", "translation": "weeping under compulsion"}, {"id": "anagkadakrys-def1", "translation": "who weeps under compulsion"}, {"id": "anagkadakrys-quote1", "translation": "weeping under compulsion, not from any passion or misfortune. Aeschylus (fr. 415)."}, {"id": "agnos-orth1", "translation": "impure"}, {"id": "agnos-def1", "translation": "impure"}, {"id": "agnos-quote1", "translation": "breathing impious, turning, impure, unholy thoughts"}, {"id": "agnos-quote2", "translation": "the impure deeds of my mother"}, {"id": "anago-orth1", "translation": "to bring back"}, {"id": "anago-def1", "translation": "to bring back"}, {"id": "anago-note1", "translation": "which the scholiast wrongly took as the future of ἀνάσσω [to be lord], interpreting it as βασιλεύσομεν [we shall rule]."}, {"id": "anago-quote1", "translation": "to bring back the upright among the dead"}, {"id": "anago-quote2", "translation": "having been brought back openly from Ilium"}, {"id": "anago-quote3", "translation": "and how shall we bring back dear Orestes to his home?"}, {"id": "anago-word1", "translation": "to be lord"}, {"id": "anago-word2", "translation": "we shall rule"}, {"id": "anadaio_see-orth1", "translation": "to kindle"}, {"id": "anadaio_see-note1", "translation": "See ἀνδαίω [to kindle]."}, {"id": "anadaio_see-word1", "translation": "to kindle"}, {"id": "anadyomai-orth1", "translation": "to emerge"}, {"id": "anadyomai-def1", "translation": "(with second aorist ἀνέδυν [I emerged]) to emerge"}, {"id": "anadyomai-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected what is in M: ανδεῖν (ἂν ἰδεῖν [to see] pr.), said by apocope for ἀναδύναι [to emerge], as δοῦν [to give] for δοῦναι [to give], on which L. Dindorf spoke in Thes. vol. 1, 2 p. 1418. The scholiast explained the corrupt reading by ἀναβλέψαι [to look up]."}, {"id": "anadyomai-quote1", "translation": "grant that he may emerge into the house of the man"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word1", "translation": "I emerged"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word2", "translation": "to see"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word3", "translation": "to emerge"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word4", "translation": "to give"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word5", "translation": "to give"}, {"id": "anadyomai-word6", "translation": "to look up"}, {"id": "anaitho-orth1", "translation": "to burn, to kindle"}, {"id": "anaitho-def1", "translation": "to burn, to kindle"}, {"id": "anaitho-note1", "translation": "Used intransitively for 'to shine forth' or 'to gleam'"}, {"id": "anaitho-note2", "translation": "Valckenaer restored it, which the scholiast seems to have read, explaining it by ἀνέλαμψαν [they shone forth]. Meineke proposed ἀνήθοντ' [they were kindled]."}, {"id": "anaitho-quote1", "translation": "and many torches were kindled (M has ἀνῆλθον [they went up]), blinded by darkness"}, {"id": "anaitho-word1", "translation": "they shone forth"}, {"id": "anaitho-word2", "translation": "they were kindled"}, {"id": "anaimaktos-orth1", "translation": "without bloodshed"}, {"id": "anaimaktos-def1", "translation": "without bloodshed"}, {"id": "anaimaktos-quote1", "translation": "these bloodless exiles"}, {"id": "anaimatos-orth1", "translation": "bloodless"}, {"id": "anaimatos-def1", "translation": "bloodless"}, {"id": "anaimatos-quote1", "translation": "a bloodless pasture of the gods"}, {"id": "anainomai-orth1", "translation": "to deny, to refuse, to reject"}, {"id": "anainomai-def1", "translation": "to deny, to refuse, to reject"}, {"id": "anainomai-note1", "translation": "With accusative"}, {"id": "anainomai-note2", "translation": "With infinitive"}, {"id": "anainomai-note3", "translation": "With participle"}, {"id": "anainomai-quote1", "translation": "the far-sent light of the watch-fire was not refused"}, {"id": "anainomai-quote2", "translation": "I do not refuse to die"}, {"id": "anainomai-quote3", "translation": "I do not refuse to be a meal for the birds"}, {"id": "anainomai-quote4", "translation": "defeated by words, I do not refuse"}, {"id": "anaireo-orth1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "anaireo-def1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "anaireo-note1", "translation": "in spurious verses"}, {"id": "anaireo-quote1", "translation": "and with this trick, killing many, he would warm his heart"}, {"id": "anaitios-orth1", "translation": "guiltless"}, {"id": "anaitios-def1", "translation": "guiltless"}, {"id": "anaitios-note1", "translation": "where Blomfield reads ἀναίτιοι [guiltless], although μεταίτιαι [sharing in guilt] and παραιτία [accessory cause] are also found in Aeschylus, on which see Lobeck, Paralip. p. 458."}, {"id": "anaitios-quote1", "translation": "you are guiltless of this murder"}, {"id": "anaitios-quote2", "translation": "guiltless of these evils"}, {"id": "anaitios-word1", "translation": "guiltless"}, {"id": "anaitios-word2", "translation": "sharing in guilt"}, {"id": "anaitios-word3", "translation": "accessory cause"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-orth1", "translation": "to call back"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-def1", "translation": "(middle form) to call back"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-def2", "translation": "to call up"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-note1", "translation": "unless here too ἀγκαλεῖσθε [you call upon] should be written"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-quote1", "translation": "who could call back the black blood of a man by chanting spells?"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-quote2", "translation": "you call upon Darius"}, {"id": "anakaleomai-word1", "translation": "you call upon"}, {"id": "anaktaomai-orth1", "translation": "to recover"}, {"id": "anaktaomai-def1", "translation": "to recover"}, {"id": "anaktaomai-quote1", "translation": "he will recover his father's house (M has ἀνακτήση [you will recover])"}, {"id": "anaktor-orth1", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "anaktor-def1", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "anaktor-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected what is in M: οἷον (οἷον [such as] schol.) ἄνακτα δαρεῖὰν ἠέ [king Dareian]"}, {"id": "anaktor-quote1", "translation": "revered king"}, {"id": "anaktor-quote2", "translation": "divine king Dareian"}, {"id": "anaktor-word1", "translation": "such as"}, {"id": "anaktor-word2", "translation": "king Dareian"}, {"id": "anakokyo-orth1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "anakokyo-def1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "anakokyo-quote1", "translation": "having lamented shrilly"}, {"id": "analios_see-orth1", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "analios_see-word1", "translation": "sunless"}, {"id": "analisko-orth1", "translation": "to consume"}, {"id": "analisko-def1", "translation": "to consume"}, {"id": "analisko-quote1", "translation": "why should one speak of those consumed in the vote?"}, {"id": "analkis-orth1", "translation": "cowardly"}, {"id": "analkis-def1", "translation": "cowardly"}, {"id": "analkis-quote1", "translation": "to be called cowardly rather than bloodthirsty"}, {"id": "analkis-quote2", "translation": "a cowardly lion"}, {"id": "analoo-orth1", "translation": "to consume"}, {"id": "analoo-def1", "translation": "same as ἀναλίσκω [to consume], to consume"}, {"id": "analoo-quote1", "translation": "and he himself consumes his ill-fated race"}, {"id": "analoo-word1", "translation": "to consume"}, {"id": "analyter-orth1", "translation": "deliverer"}, {"id": "analyter-def1", "translation": "deliverer"}, {"id": "analyter-note1", "translation": "The same is ἀλλύτας [deliverer] (i.e. ἀναλύτης [deliverer]), which see."}, {"id": "analyter-quote1", "translation": "deliverer of the house"}, {"id": "analyter-word1", "translation": "deliverer"}, {"id": "analyter-word2", "translation": "deliverer"}, {"id": "analoma-orth1", "translation": "expense, loss"}, {"id": "analoma-def1", "translation": "expense, loss"}, {"id": "analoma-quote1", "translation": "how is the expense not bitter?"}, {"id": "anameno-orth1", "translation": "to await"}, {"id": "anameno-def1", "translation": "to await"}, {"id": "anameno-quote1", "translation": "I will await"}, {"id": "anamix-orth1", "translation": "mixed together"}, {"id": "anamix-def1", "translation": "mixed together"}, {"id": "anamix-note1", "translation": "Heimsoeth proposed άμμιγα [mixed together]"}, {"id": "anamix-word1", "translation": "mixed together"}, {"id": "anamplaketos-orth1", "translation": "not to be missed"}]}